  "style": {
    "id": "hanging-mobile",
    "name": "Hanging Mobile",
    "description": "A kinetic hanging mobile in a bright skylit gallery: thin black wire arms with end loops, fine threads and flat painted sheet-metal plates (disc, leaf, crescent, triangle, custom outlines) in bold red, yellow, blue, black and white turn slowly in still air, while crisp soft shadows drift across the white wall behind. Balance is computed for real: every arm's pivot is solved from the weights on each side (weight = plate area), so hanging a new shape or changing a weight tilts that arm and every arm above it, the whole structure swings and re-settles with a closed-form damped oscillation, and a re-balance slides each pivot loop to the new centre. Small engraved tags hang under the plates; a museum-label overlay carries the words.",
